The main objective is to convert raw e-commerce transaction data into meaningful business insights using Power BI.

The project follows this overall process:

Business Understanding → Data Understanding → Data Cleaning → Data Modeling → KPI Definition → DAX → Dashboard → Business Insights → Recommendations

The final goal is not just to create charts, but to help management understand sales, customers, products, orders, payments, and customer retention so that they can make data-driven business decisions.

1. Business Areas Covered

The project analyzes five major areas:
| Area               | What we analyze                                            |
| ------------------ | ---------------------------------------------------------- |
| Sales Performance  | Revenue, orders, AOV, sales trends                         |
| Customer Analytics | Customers, new customers, repeat customers, customer value |
| Product & Category | Product sales, category revenue, stock, pricing            |
| Orders & Payments  | Delivered/cancelled orders, payment methods, cancellation  |
| Customer Retention | Repeat purchases, customer segments, customer value        |


2. Dataset / Tables

The project contains four main business entities:

Customers → Orders → Order Items ← Products
| Table       | Purpose                                       |
| ----------- | --------------------------------------------- |
| Customers   | Customer profile and registration information |
| Products    | Product details, categories, prices and stock |
| Orders      | Order-level information                       |
| Order Items | Products purchased within each order          |

3. Data Cleaning

Before analysis, the data must be checked and cleaned using Power Query.

Important checks include:

Duplicate records
Missing values
Invalid dates
Invalid prices
Incorrect quantities
Inconsistent categories
Inconsistent cities
Invalid customer/product/order IDs
Unexpected payment methods
Unexpected order statuses

4.Data Modeling

After cleaning, relationships are created between the tables.

Basic model:

Customers
    │
    │ Customer_ID
    ▼
 Orders
    │
    │ Order_ID
    ▼
Order Items
    │
    │ Product_ID
    ▼
Products

